// An inline lambda body is an expression, and assignment is also an expression
// here, so 'proc(): y = 7' parses as '(proc(): y) = 7' -- the '=' binds outside
// the body.  The error should say that rather than blaming the left-hand side.
// Parenthesising, 'proc(): (y = 7)', is the one-line fix; the block form works
// too.
var y = 0
var p = proc(): y = 7
p()
